<title>USA: Ashland restores Minnesota crude unit.</title>
<headline>Ashland restores Minnesota crude unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashland Inc restored over the weekend a 70,000 barrel per day crude distillation unit at its St Paul, Minnesota refinery that had been downed by a fire, an Ashland spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's up and running,&quot; said Ashland spokesman Chuck Rice.</p>
<p>He said the fire minorly damaged some electrical equipment, and that the plant was now running at commercial rates.</p>
<p>((-- New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1633))</p>
